From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:28:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: Add TYHX HX32062SE ambient light and proximity
 sensor

Add a driver for the TYHX HX32062SE, an ambient light and infrared
proximity sensor found on the Zinwa Q25.

There is no public datasheet. The register sequences are those the
vendor sensor-hub firmware uses for this part (chip ID 0x37):

 - a fixed initialisation sequence followed by ALS gain setting 1;
 - a proximity gain and an ALS dark offset derived from the factory
   fuses at 0x92/0x95/0x97, which the chip loads itself and which are
   never written;
 - a hold bit in 0x83 that latches the data registers for a coherent
   multi-byte read;
 - a restart pulse on 0x1a bit 2 after enabling, and a second one once
   the proximity engine has produced its first frames.

The ALS channel reports the offset-corrected 24-bit count with the
vendor firmware's lux conversion as the scale. The proximity channel
reports the raw 16-bit reflectance count, and nearlevel comes from the
proximity-near-level property as for other IIO proximity sensors.

The vendor firmware polls this part; its interrupt output was not seen
to reach an application processor pin on the Q25, so the driver polls
too and offers no events. The sensor is powered on through runtime PM
when a channel is read, with a five-second autosuspend delay because
the proximity engine needs 250 ms to produce data after enabling.

Signed-off-by: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
